Third-party components

The pure-Rust workspace replaces the former C++ dependencies:

- SSH, SFTP and SCP transport, jump tunnels and host-key handling via `russh`
  and `russh-sftp` (Apache-2.0), key parsing via `ssh-key`/`ssh-encoding` (MIT/Apache-2.0).
- Cryptography: `argon2` (MIT), `aes`/`cbc` (MIT/Apache-2.0), `hmac`/`sha1`/`sha2`/`pbkdf2`
  (MIT/Apache-2.0), `base64` (MIT/Apache-2.0), `zeroize` (MIT/Apache-2.0),
  `bcrypt-pbkdf` (MIT/Apache-2.0), `ed25519-dalek`/`p256`/`p384`/`p521` (BSD/Apache-2.0),
  `crc32fast`/`md-5` (MIT/Apache-2.0). PPK v2/v3 and `lscp1$` session encryption live in
  `crates/linscp-crypto`.
- TLS: `rustls` (Apache-2.0/MIT/ISC) with `ring` (ISC) and `webpki-roots`
  (MPL-2.0), `tokio-rustls` (MIT/Apache-2.0), `rustls-pki-types` (MIT/Apache-2.0),
  custom `ServerCertVerifier` wrapping `WebPkiServerVerifier` for SPKI pinning and
  Min/MaxTlsVersion enforcement.
- HTTP/WebDAV/S3: `reqwest` (MIT/Apache-2.0), `hyper` (MIT), `http` (MIT/Apache-2.0),
  `quick-xml` (MIT), `bytes` (MIT), `http-body` (MIT).
- FTP/FTPS: `suppaftp` (Apache-2.0/MIT) with native Unix/DOS/VMS LIST + MLSD parser
  (`crates/linscp-proto/src/listing.rs`).
- Async runtime: `tokio` (MIT).
- Local filesystem & platform: `crossterm` (MIT), `portable-pty` (MIT), `notify`
  (CC0/MIT), `encoding_rs` (BSD-3-Clause), `filetime` (MIT/Apache-2.0).
- HTTP server mode: `axum` (MIT), `tower` (MIT), `tokio-tungstenite` (MIT/Apache-2.0),
  `serde`/`serde_json` (MIT/Apache-2.0).
- Tauri v2 desktop/mobile shell (`crates/linscp-tauri`) and plugins: `tauri`
  (MIT/Apache-2.0), `tauri-plugin-dialog`/`fs`/`shell` (MIT/Apache-2.0).
- UI: TypeScript + `esbuild` (MIT), and the browser terminal embeds xterm.js 6.0.0
  and its FitAddon (source/gui/web/vendor/, MIT licence; full notice in
  vendor/LICENSE-xterm.txt) now vendored under `ui/src/vendor/` and `ui/vendor/`
  where applicable, bundled via `ui/scripts/build.mjs`.

All Rust crates are listed with exact versions and licenses in `Cargo.lock`;
a `cargo-about`/`cargo-deny` report can be generated with `cargo about generate`.

The browser terminal in the graphical client embeds xterm.js 6.0.0 and
its FitAddon (MIT licence; the full notice is in
ui/vendor/LICENSE-xterm.txt or source/gui/web/vendor/LICENSE-xterm.txt).

